<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to June 25 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.44 (0.44)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.58 (0.62)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  1.02 (1.06)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.39 (0.39)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.53 (0.57)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.98 (1.02)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.35 (0.34)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.48 (0.52)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.25)	 three years  0.93 (0.97)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Jun 23 - Jun 27:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.59 (0.57)   120-150 days  0.64 (0.65)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.59 (0.58)   150-180 days  0.71 (0.68)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.60 (0.59)   180-360 days  0.68 (0.68)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.62 (0.60)   over 360 days 0.88 (0.76)</p>
